---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import SectionNav from '../components/SectionNav.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import FactStrip from '../components/FactStrip.astro';
import Warnings from '../components/Warnings.astro';
import Timeline from '../components/Timeline.astro';
import PlaceGrid from '../components/PlaceGrid.astro';
import PinList from '../components/PinList.astro';
import DayStatus from '../components/DayStatus.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { FACTS, WARNINGS, PLAN, SPECIALITIES, SUNSET } from '../data/mykonos-essentials';
import { MYKONOS_SIGHTS, MYKONOS_FOOD, MYKONOS_PINS } from '../data/mykonos-places';

const nav = [
  { id: 'day', label: 'The day' },
  { id: 'ashore', label: 'Getting ashore' },
  { id: 'see', label: 'See' },
  { id: 'eat', label: 'Eat' },
  { id: 'know', label: 'Know this' },
];

const sights = MYKONOS_SIGHTS.filter((p) => p.kind !== 'shop');
const shops = MYKONOS_SIGHTS.filter((p) => p.kind === 'shop');
---

<Base
  title="Mykonos — Liv's Islands"
  description="One day in Mykonos Town on foot: the windmills, Little Venice, the alleys and where to eat. Thursday 22 October 2026."
  themeColor="#0d3a5c"
>
  <Hero
    backHref="/"
    eyebrow="Thursday 22 October · 07:00 – 17:00"
    title="Mykonos"
    accent="all within 400 metres"
    lede="The tender drops you in the middle of the thing you came to see. No bus, no shuttle, no transfer — every famous sight is a five-minute walk from the pier."
    imageId="mykonos-hero"
    alt="The row of windmills at Kato Mili above Mykonos Town"
  >
    <DayStatus date="2026-10-22" fallback="Thursday 22 October" />
  </Hero>

  <SectionNav items={nav} />

  <main id="main">
    <Section
      id="day"
      eyebrow="At a glance"
      title="The numbers that matter"
      lede="A shorter day than Santorini, and the clock is the whole game."
    >
      <FactStrip facts={FACTS} />

      <div class="plan" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="plan__h">Front-load everything</h3>
        <p class="plan__p">
          Paraportiani and Little Venice are empty at 08:15 and unbearable by
          noon, and you sail before the sunset everyone else is waiting for.
          So do the famous things first, in the morning light, and spend the
          middle of the day in the alleys where the crowd doesn't matter.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Timeline legs={PLAN} />
    </Section>

    <Section
      id="ashore"
      tone="sunk"
      eyebrow="The bit that goes wrong"
      title="Getting ashore, and back"
      lede="Another tender port — the ship is too big for the quay, so she anchors and you ride in."
    >
      <div class="prose stack" data-reveal>
        <h3>Two landing points, and you don't pick</h3>
        <p>
          The port authority and the ship decide. Best case is the town pier by
          the Town Hall, where you step off directly into Chora. The other is the
          old port bus station end, which is a flat ten to twelve minute walk
          south-west along the water — still no shuttle needed, but
          <strong>shift every leg of the day twelve minutes earlier</strong> if
          that's where you land.
        </p>
        <p>
          A new tender berth at the old port was finished in May 2026 and may be
          in service for your call, which can only make the landing better.
        </p>

        <h3>The deadline, honestly</h3>
        <p>
          The ship sails at 17:00, but that is not your deadline. Tendering eats
          thirty to forty-five minutes at each end, and the last-tender queue is
          the longest of the day. <strong>Be in the queue by 15:45</strong> and
          treat whatever time the Cruise Compass prints as half an hour earlier
          than printed. The forty-five minutes that buys you is the plan, not
          slack.
        </p>

        <h3>Don't bother with a beach</h3>
        <p>
          The sea is about 20°C, the beach clubs have shut for the season, and
          Ornos or Platys Gialos costs you two and a half to three hours of an
          eight-hour day on an hourly winter bus — miss one and you cannot get
          that back against a hard tender time. If you want your feet in the sea,
          walk to Megali Ammos instead. It's close enough to be safe.
        </p>
      </div>

      <PinList title="Pin these before you lose signal" pins={MYKONOS_PINS} />
    </Section>

    <Section
      id="see"
      eyebrow="Morning"
      title="What to actually see"
      lede="All of it inside a four-hundred-metre circle, which is why the day works at all."
    >
      <PlaceGrid places={sights} />
      <h3 class="sub">Worth going into</h3>
      <PlaceGrid places={shops} />
    </Section>

    <Section
      id="eat"
      tone="sky"
      eyebrow="Midday"
      title="Where to eat"
      lede="Most of the famous restaurants here open at 19:00 and are useless to you. These are open while you're ashore."
    >
      <PlaceGrid places={MYKONOS_FOOD} />

      <h3 class="sub">Order these</h3>
      <ul class="specs">
        {SPECIALITIES.map((s, i) => (
          <li class="spec" style={`--reveal-delay:${i * 45}ms;`} data-reveal>
            <h4 class="spec__name">
              {s.name}
              {s.greek && <span class="spec__greek" lang="el">{s.greek}</span>}
            </h4>
            <p class="spec__what">{s.what}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </Section>

    <Section
      id="know"
      tone="sunk"
      eyebrow="Before you step off"
      title="Five things that decide the day"
    >
      <Warnings items={WARNINGS} />

      <div class="prose stack" data-reveal>
        <h3>Everything else, briefly</h3>
        <ul class="plain">
          <li>
            <strong>Sunset is {SUNSET}</strong>, and you'll be aboard about ninety
            minutes before it. Anyone telling you Mykonos sunsets in October are
            at half five is an hour wrong — the clocks don't change until the
            25th.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Water.</strong> Don't drink the tap water. Buy bottled, and
            buy some for the tender queue before you walk down.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>There is no good bookshop</strong> in Mykonos Town. Don't
            spend any of the day looking for one.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Most "best of Mykonos" restaurant lists are dinner-only</strong>
            — To Maereio, m-eating, Kalita and the rest open at 19:00. If you walk
            past To Maereio on Kalogera, read the door anyway; it costs nothing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Greek October is kind here.</strong> Royal Caribbean's own
            guidance says most shops and restaurants stay open through the month.
            Some won't be. Have a second option for lunch.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The Greek on the Santorini page works here too</strong> —
            same country, same please and thank you.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p><a class="xlink" href="/santorini">The Santorini page &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
    </Section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .prose h3 { font-size: var(--step-2); margin-block-start: var(--sp-lg); }
  .prose h3:first-child { margin-block-start: 0; }
  .prose p { color: var(--fg-soft); }
  .prose strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 650; }

  .plain { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-sm); padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .plain li {
    padding-inline-start: var(--sp-md);
    border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--fg-soft);
  }
  .plain strong { color: var(--fg); }

  .plan { max-width: var(--measure); margin-block: var(--sp-xl) var(--sp-lg); }
  .plan__h { font-size: var(--step-2); margin-block-end: var(--sp-xs); }
  .plan__p { color: var(--fg-soft); }

  .sub { margin-block: var(--sp-xl) var(--sp-md); font-size: var(--step-2); }

  .xlink { font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }

  .specs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 15rem), 1fr));
    gap: var(--sp-md);
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .spec {
    padding: var(--sp-md);
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    background: var(--bg-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sh-sm);
  }
  .spec__name {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-block-end: 0.3rem;
  }
  .spec__greek {
    font-family: var(--font-text);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--fg-soft);
    opacity: 0.75;
  }
  .spec__what { font-size: var(--step-0); color: var(--fg-soft); line-height: 1.5; }
</style>
